Changes from the upstream plugin:
- Autodesk Fusion, the upstream plugin's one CAD connector, is replaced by a different
  CAD system (SOLIDWORKS or Onshape, per edition) through a bridge in servers/.
- Text in the skills that named Fusion is changed to the edition's CAD system, and
  steps the bridge cannot do yet (building models from drawings, STEP import, CAM)
  are marked as not available, with the hand-entered fallback the upstream plugin
  already defines.
- The changes are made by tools/cad-variants/build.py in the fork that carries this folder.

